 "answer": "**Part A:**\nStarting balance = 1200.00\nTransactions for months 1 to 15:\nRule each month: Balance = Balance + Transaction. If Balance < 1500, Balance = Balance - 15. Then Balance = Balance * 1.0025.\n\n- Month 1: 1200 + 1100 = 2300. >= 1500, fee = 0. Interest: 2300 * 1.0025 = 2305.75\n- Month 2: 2305.75 - 250 = 2055.75. >= 1500. Interest: 2055.75 * 1.0025 = 2060.889375\n- Month 3: 2060.889375 + 300 = 2360.889375. >= 1500. Interest: 2360.889375 * 1.0025 = 2366.791598\n- Month 4: 2366.791598 - 650 = 1716.791598. >= 1500. Interest: 1716.791598 * 1.0025 = 1721.083577\n- Month 5: 1721.083577 - 650 = 1071.083577. < 1500, fee -15 -> 1056.083577. Interest: 1056.083577 * 1.0025 = 1058.723786\n- Month 6: 1058.723786 - 900 = 158.723786. < 1500, fee -15 -> 143.723786. Interest: 143.723786 * 1.0025 = 144.083095\n- Month 7: 144.083095 + 1100 = 1244.083095. < 1500, fee -15 -> 1229.083095. Interest: 1229.083095 * 1.0025 = 1232.155803\n- Month 8: 1232.155803 - 400 = 832.155803. < 1500, fee -15 -> 817.155803. Interest: 817.155803 * 1.0025 = 819.198693\n- Month 9: 819.198693 + 450 = 1269.198693. < 1500, fee -15 -> 1254.198693. Interest: 1254.198693 * 1.0025 = 1257.334190\n- Month 10: 1257.334190 - 900 = 357.334190. < 1500, fee -15 -> 342.334190. Interest: 342.334190 * 1.0025 = 343.189995\n- Month 11: 343.189995 + 700 = 1043.189995. < 1500, fee -15 -> 1028.189995. Interest: 1028.189995 * 1.0025 = 1030.760470\n- Month 12: 1030.760470 - 250 = 780.760470. < 1500, fee -15 -> 765.760470. Interest: 765.760470 * 1.0025 = 767.674871\n- Month 13: 767.674871 - 400 = 367.674871. < 1500, fee -15 -> 352.674871. Interest: 352.674871 * 1.0025 = 353.556558\n- Month 14: 353.556558 + 1100 = 1453.556558. < 1500, fee -15 -> 1438.556558. Interest: 1438.556558 * 1.0025 = 1442.152949\n- Month 15: 1442.152949 - 400 = 1042.152949. < 1500, fee -15 -> 1027.152949. Interest: 1027.152949 * 1.0025 = 1029.720831\n\nRounding to the nearest cent: 1029.72\n\n**Part B:**\nFind the smallest positive integer $x$ such that:\n$x \\equiv 11 \\pmod{19}$\n$x \\equiv 9 \\pmod{16}$\n$x \\equiv 8 \\pmod{13}$\n\nFrom $x \\equiv 9 \\pmod{16}$:\n$x = 16k + 9$\n$16k + 9 \\equiv 11 \\pmod{19} \\implies -3k \\equiv 2 \\pmod{19} \\implies 3k \\equiv -2 \\equiv 17 \\pmod{19} \\implies 3k \\equiv 36 \\pmod{19} \\implies k \\equiv 12 \\pmod{19}$.\nSo $x = 16(19m + 12) + 9 = 304m + 201$.\nNow, $x \\equiv 8 \\pmod{13}$:\n$304m + 201 \\equiv 8 \\pmod{13}$\n$304 = 23 \\times 13 + 5 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{13}$\n$201 = 15 \\times 13 + 6 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{13}$\n$5m + 6 \\equiv 8 \\implies 5m \\equiv 2 \\equiv 15 \\pmod{13} \\implies m \\equiv 3 \\pmod{13}$.\nSmallest positive integer is for $m = 3$:\n$x = 304(3) + 201 = 912 + 201 = 1113$.\n\nCheck:\n1113 / 19 = 58 R 11.\n1113 / 16 = 69 R 9.\n1113 / 13 = 85 R 8.\n\n**Part C:**\nIntegers $n \\in \\{1, \\dots, 8000\\}$.\nCondition: divisible by at least one of 6, 10, or 15, and not divisible by 17.\nDivisible by at least one of 6, 10, 15 is the set of multiples of 6, 10, 15.\nLet $S$ be the union of multiples of 6, 10, 15:\n$|S| = \\lfloor 8000/6 \\rfloor + \\lfloor 8000/10 \\rfloor + \\lfloor 8000/15 \\rfloor - \\lfloor 8000/\\text{lcm}(6,10) \\rfloor - \\lfloor 8000/\\text{lcm}(6,15) \\rfloor - \\lfloor 8000/\\text{lcm}(10,15) \\rfloor + \\lfloor 8000/\\text{lcm}(6,10,15) \\rfloor$\n$\\text{lcm}(6,10) = 30$, $\\text{lcm}(6,15) = 30$, $\\text{lcm}(10,15) = 30$, $\\text{lcm}(6,10,15) = 30$.\nSo $|S| = \\lfloor 8000/6 \\rfloor + \\lfloor 8000/10 \\rfloor + \\lfloor 8000/15 \\rfloor - 3 \\lfloor 8000/30 \\rfloor + \\lfloor 8000/30 \\rfloor$\n$= 1333 + 800 + 533 - 2(266) = 2666 - 532 = 2134$.\n\nNow subtract those also divisible by 17:\nDivisible by 17 and (6, 10, or 15) means divisible by at least one of $\\text{lcm}(6,17)=102$, $\\text{lcm}(10,17)=170$, $\\text{lcm}(15,17)=255$.\nTheir pairwise and triple LCMs are all $\\text{lcm}(30, 17) = 510$.\n$|S \\cap M_{17}| = \\lfloor 8000/102 \\rfloor + \\lfloor 8000/170 \\rfloor + \\lfloor 8000/255 \\rfloor - 2\\lfloor 8000/510 \\rfloor$\n$\\lfloor 8000/102 \\rfloor = 78$\n$\\lfloor 8000/170 \\rfloor = 47$\n$\\lfloor 8000/255 \\rfloor = 31$\n$\\lfloor 8000/510 \\rfloor = 15$\n$|S \\cap M_{17}| = 78 + 47 + 31 - 2(15) = 156 - 30 = 126$.\n\nTotal = $2134 - 126 = 2008$.\n\nFINAL: 1029.72; 1113; 2008"
